    "db_emissionrateadjustment": {
      "kind": "static",
      "source": {
        "url_template": "./movesdb/EmissionRateAdjustment.parquet"
      },
      "extent": {
        "metaparameter": "n_emissionrateadjustment"
      },
      "metadata": {
        "tags": [
          "adjustment"
        ],
        "note": "EmissionRateAdjustment, the national table: 1131 rows against the 241 the execution-database copy held, and the copy is a strict subset of it -- every one of its rows is in this file, value for value. What the run selects from it is in the joins. 26 of the 1131 carry a factor that is not 1 and reach a model year this corpus runs; every one of those is heavy-duty ELECTRIC running energy, which is why `expand-sourcetype` is the first RunSpec here that can tell the table is read.",
        "esio_format": "parquet"
      }
    },
    "db_regioncounty": {
      "kind": "static",
      "source": {
        "url_template": "./movesdb/regionCounty.parquet"
      },
      "extent": {
        "metaparameter": "n_regioncounty"
      },
      "metadata": {
        "tags": [
          "fuel",
          "scope"
        ],
        "note": "regionCounty, the national table: 407,233 rows -- every (region, county, regionCode, fuelYear) pairing MOVES ships, and the biggest table this document reads after the two rate tables. It is read for ONE number per county: the fuel region whose `fuelSupply` rows the county's formulations come from. `regionCodeID` 1 is the onroad refinery supply and 2 the nonroad one, so the gather filters to 1; a document that dropped that filter would pick up whichever of the two rows the sum reached first.",
        "esio_format": "parquet"
      }
    },
    "db_fuelsupply": {
      "kind": "static",
      "source": {
        "url_template": "./movesdb/FuelSupply.parquet"
      },
      "extent": {
        "metaparameter": "n_fuelsupply"
      },
      "metadata": {
        "tags": [
          "fuel"
        ],
        "note": "FuelSupply, the national table: 105,651 rows. The (fuelRegion, fuelYear, monthGroup) -> (formulation, marketShare) relation. `marketShare` is a WEIGHT on the rate and not on the formulation's properties -- `baseratecalculator/aggregate.rs:38` accumulates `mean_base_rate * market_share` -- so a fuel effect that multiplies the rate may be weighted by it BEFORE the rate is touched, which is what J60 does. Every county in this corpus supplies exactly one formulation per fuel type at share 1.0, so the corpus cannot tell that ordering from any other (conventions §23); the linearity is the argument, not the measurement.",
        "esio_format": "parquet"
      }
    },
    "db_fuelformulation": {
      "kind": "static",
      "source": {
        "url_template": "./movesdb/FuelFormulation.parquet"
      },
      "extent": {
        "metaparameter": "n_fuelformulation"
      },
      "metadata": {
        "tags": [
          "fuel"
        ],
        "note": "FuelFormulation, the national table: 2,158 rows, read for seven of its seventeen property columns -- the six the running-exhaust criteria polynomial uses and the one the biodiesel form uses. THE COLUMNS CARRY NULLS AND A NULL ARRIVES AS A NaN: 2,118 rows have a NULL `BioDieselEsterVolume`, 7 a NULL `T50`, 6 a NULL `RVP`, `ETOHVolume` and `aromaticContent`, and 1 a NULL `T90`. MOVES sweeps them with `changeFuelFormulationNulls`; so does this document, through lib/fuel_effects.esm's `fuel_property_or_zero`, and without it one NaN formulation would poison a market-share sum that never selected it. THE VALUES ARE THE DECIMALS AND NOT THE binary32 WIDENINGS. MariaDB stores these columns as FLOAT and MOVES computes in DOUBLE, so the number that entered MOVES's arithmetic was 23.139999389648438 where this table says 23.14 (docs/fuel-effects-generator.md §7.2). The gap is 4.4e-08 on the criteria ratio, measured; tolerance.toml's per-cell bound is 2e-05, so no fixture here can see it, and components/fuel_effects.esm is where the question is decided.",
        "esio_format": "parquet"
      }
    },
    "db_fuelsubtype": {
      "kind": "static",
      "source": {
        "url_template": "./movesdb/FuelSubtype.parquet"
      },
      "extent": {
        "metaparameter": "n_fuelsubtype"
      },
      "metadata": {
        "tags": [
          "fuel"
        ],
        "note": "FuelSubtype, the national table: 15 rows. Read for `fuelTypeID`, which is how a formulation reaches the fuel type its rate rows are keyed by. Two of the subtypes `FuelFormulation` uses -- 23 and 24 -- are NOT in this table, so their formulations gather fuel type 0 and match no criteria row; neither is in any fuel supply this corpus selects.",
        "esio_format": "parquet"
      }
    },
    "db_e10fuelproperties": {
      "kind": "static",
      "source": {
        "url_template": "./movesdb/e10FuelProperties.parquet"
      },
      "extent": {
        "metaparameter": "n_e10fuelproperties"
      },
      "metadata": {
        "tags": [
          "fuel"
        ],
        "note": "e10FuelProperties, the national table: 16,117 rows over 24 fuel regions, 64 fuel years and 13 month groups. This is the table that makes an E85 formulation computable at all. The default database ships the high-ethanol formulations with DISTILLATION SENTINELS -- formulation 27002 has `T50` 999, `T90` 999 and `ETOHVolume` 74 -- and the THC criteria polynomial carries `5.58e-05*T50*T50`, so reading them straight returns a ratio of 1.0e+17 instead of 0.64. `FuelEffectsGenerator.setup()` step 020 (`alterHighEthanolFuelProperties`) overwrites every combustion property of a subtype-51 or -52 formulation with this table's row for the formulation's own (region, fuelYear, monthGroup), falling back to the national row 0 and then to the formulation's own value. RVP is NOT overwritten -- it is the one property the E85 row keeps, and the e10 RVP goes to a separate `altRVP` column that only `altCriteriaRatio` reads. NOT ONE of the 15,360 non-national rows has a NULL in any of the six columns read here, so the fallback chain collapses to the region's own row wherever one exists; the national row 0, by contrast, has a NULL `sulfurLevel` and `ETOHVolume` in all 757 of its rows, which is what the fallback would be falling back to.",
        "esio_format": "parquet"
      }
    },
    "db_complexmodelparameters": {
      "kind": "static",
      "source": {
        "url_template": "./movesdb/ComplexModelParameters.parquet"
      },
      "extent": {
        "metaparameter": "n_complexmodelparameters"
      },
      "metadata": {
        "tags": [
          "fuel"
        ],
        "note": "ComplexModelParameters, the national table: 1,090 rows. The EPA Complex Model's polynomial: one coefficient per (pollutant-process, fuel model, complex-model parameter). THE COEFFICIENT IS `coeff1 + coeff2 + coeff3` and not `coeff1` -- three columns that are summed, not three alternatives, and reading the first alone leaves CO wrong by 5.6e-03 (`criteria.rs:639`). All 241 rows the three running-exhaust pollutant-processes use are non-zero, so canonical's `if coeff == 0 { continue }` has nothing to skip here.",
        "esio_format": "parquet"
      }
    },
    "db_meanfuelparameters": {
      "kind": "static",
      "source": {
        "url_template": "./movesdb/MeanFuelParameters.parquet"
      },
      "extent": {
        "metaparameter": "n_meanfuelparameters"
      },
      "metadata": {
        "tags": [
          "fuel"
        ],
        "note": "MeanFuelParameters, the national table: 264 rows. The centering and standardising constants each complex-model property is measured against, per (pollutant-process, fuel type, model-year group). BOTH COLUMNS CARRY NULLS AND THE TWO NULLS MEAN DIFFERENT THINGS: a NULL `centeringValue` is no centering (0), a NULL `stdDevValue` is no standardising (1), and every `stdDevValue` for CO is NULL while every `centeringValue` for CO is not. A property with no row at all -- `HI` and `Intercept` have none -- takes (0, 1) as well, which is the `exact_else_wildcard` below.",
        "esio_format": "parquet"
      }
    },
    "db_fuelmodelwtfactor": {
      "kind": "static",
      "source": {
        "url_template": "./movesdb/FuelModelWtFactor.parquet"
      },
      "extent": {
        "metaparameter": "n_fuelmodelwtfactor"
      },
      "metadata": {
        "tags": [
          "fuel"
        ],
        "note": "FuelModelWtFactor, the national table: 1,804 rows. The weight each fuel model carries in the complex model's sum, per (fuel model, model-year group, ageID). THE AGE KEY IS WHY THE COMPLEX MODEL RATIO DEPENDS ON THE COHORT AND NOT ONLY ON THE FUEL: the CO engine's weights are age-specific at model-year group 19502000, and the two predictive engines carry no 19502000 rows at all and fall back to the uniform group 0 -- which is `setFuelModelWtFactorVariables`'s own lookup order, and is measured here: 410 rows at 19502000 for the ten CO fuel models, 0 for the nine predictive ones, 369 at group 0 for those nine.",
        "esio_format": "parquet"
      }
    },
    "db_basefuel": {
      "kind": "static",
      "source": {
        "url_template": "./movesdb/BaseFuel.parquet"
      },
      "extent": {
        "metaparameter": "n_basefuel"
      },
      "metadata": {
        "tags": [
          "fuel"
        ],
        "note": "BaseFuel, the national table: 10 rows. The formulation each calculation engine measures its ratio AGAINST: formulation 99, `High Sulfur Gasoline`, for model-year group 19502000 and 98, `Low Sulfur Gasoline`, for 2001 and later. This is what makes `criteriaRatio` a ratio, and it is also why the captured table carries rows for formulations 98 and 99 whose ratio is exactly 1 -- the base fuel measured against itself. `calculationEngine` is a TEXT column with three values, decoded by a `codes` map on the binding.",
        "esio_format": "parquet"
      }
    },
    "db_sulfurmodelcoeff": {
      "kind": "static",
      "source": {
        "url_template": "./movesdb/SulfurModelCoeff.parquet"
      },
      "extent": {
        "metaparameter": "n_sulfurmodelcoeff"
      },
      "metadata": {
        "tags": [
          "fuel"
        ],
        "note": "SulfurModelCoeff, the national table: 2,340 rows. The sulfur model, keyed by (process, pollutant, M6 emitter class, SOURCE TYPE, fuel model-year group). Two emitter classes -- Normal and High -- are blended 50/50, and the model-year group is encoded IN its identifier: `19972000` is 1997 to 2000. `sulfurCoeff` holds two different quantities in one column, an exponent for the log-log function and a per-ppm rate for the log-linear one, which is why it is declared unitless and the sulfur level is divided by 1 ppm before it reaches either.",
        "esio_format": "parquet"
      }
    },
    "db_sulfurmodelname": {
      "kind": "static",
      "source": {
        "url_template": "./movesdb/SulfurModelName.parquet"
      },
      "extent": {
        "metaparameter": "n_sulfurmodelname"
      },
      "metadata": {
        "tags": [
          "fuel"
        ],
        "note": "SulfurModelName, the national table: 4 rows. Which of the two sulfur functions each (emitter, function) pairing is -- `log-log` or `log-linear` -- decoded to 1 and 0 by a `codes` map, the same way `noxhumidityadjust.humidityNOxEq` is. An EQUATION carried as data, again.",
        "esio_format": "parquet"
      }
    },
    "db_hourday": {
      "kind": "static",
      "source": {
        "url_template": "./movesdb/HourDay.parquet"
      },
      "extent": {
        "metaparameter": "n_hourday"
      },
      "metadata": {
        "tags": [
          "output"
        ],
        "note": "HourDay, the national table: 48 rows against the 24 the execution-database copy held. What the run selects from it is in the joins.",
        "esio_format": "parquet"
      }
    },
    "db_dayofanyweek": {
      "kind": "static",
      "source": {
        "url_template": "./movesdb/DayOfAnyWeek.parquet"
      },
      "extent": {
        "metaparameter": "n_dayofanyweek"
      },
      "metadata": {
        "tags": [
          "output"
        ],
        "note": "DayOfAnyWeek, the national table: 2 rows against the 1 the execution-database copy held. What the run selects from it is in the joins.",
        "esio_format": "parquet"
      }
    },
    "db_emissionprocess": {
      "kind": "static",
      "source": {
        "url_template": "./movesdb/EmissionProcess.parquet"
      },
      "extent": {
        "metaparameter": "n_emissionprocess"
      },
      "metadata": {
        "tags": [
          "scope"
        ],
        "note": "EmissionProcess: MOVES's own statement of which processes happen on a real road. `occursOnRealRoads` is what decides whether a selected pollutant-process produces output rows at all -- start exhaust and extended idle write their rates on the off-network road type 1, and a RunSpec that does not select road type 1 discards those blocks entire (docs/mixed-onroad.md 0.2). The national table has 25 rows; the execution-database copy has the 2 this run touches.",
        "esio_format": "parquet"
      }
    },
    "db_pm10emissionratio": {
      "kind": "static",
      "source": {
        "url_template": "./movesdb/PM10EmissionRatio.parquet"
      },
      "extent": {
        "metaparameter": "n_pm10emissionratio"
      },
      "metadata": {
        "tags": [
          "chain"
        ],
        "note": "PM10EmissionRatio, the national table: 530 rows against the 4 the execution-database copy held. What the run selects from it is in the joins.",
        "esio_format": "parquet"
      }
    },
    "db_nono2ratio": {
      "kind": "static",
      "source": {
        "url_template": "./movesdb/NONO2Ratio.parquet"
      },
      "extent": {
        "metaparameter": "n_nono2ratio"
      },
      "metadata": {
        "tags": [
          "chain"
        ],
        "note": "NONO2Ratio, the national table: 10,767 rows. It is the chain table for NO, NO2 and HONO exactly as PM10EmissionRatio is for PM10, and it is keyed by a model-year GROUP where that one is keyed by a model-year RANGE. It carries fuel types 1, 2, 3 and 5 and no row for electricity, which is why a species block is 104 cohorts where its parent is 124.",
        "esio_format": "parquet"
      }
    },
    "db_crankcaseemissionratio": {
      "kind": "static",
      "source": {
        "url_template": "./movesdb/CrankcaseEmissionRatio.parquet"
      },
      "extent": {
        "metaparameter": "n_crankcaseemissionratio"
      },
      "metadata": {
        "tags": [
          "chain"
        ],
        "note": "CrankcaseEmissionRatio, the national table: 20,915 rows. The third chain table, and the third way of saying which model years a ratio covers -- PM10EmissionRatio uses a min/max RANGE, NONO2Ratio a model-year GROUP, and this one a range again but with a regulatory class in the key. Fuel types 1, 2, 3 and 5, no electricity row.",
        "esio_format": "parquet"
      }
    },
    "db_methanethcratio": {
      "kind": "static",
      "source": {
        "url_template": "./movesdb/methaneTHCRatio.parquet"
      },
      "extent": {
        "metaparameter": "n_methanethcratio"
      },
      "metadata": {
        "tags": [
          "chain"
        ],
        "note": "methaneTHCRatio, the national table: 1,117 rows. The methane fraction of THC, keyed by (processID, fuel SUBTYPE, regulatory class, model-year range). It produces TWO species from one row -- methane is THC times the ratio, NMHC is THC times its complement -- and it carries fuel subtypes 10 to 52 and no row for electricity, which is why the hydrocarbon blocks are 104 cohorts where THC is 124.",
        "esio_format": "parquet"
      }
    },
    "db_hcspeciation": {
      "kind": "static",
      "source": {
        "url_template": "./movesdb/HCSpeciation.parquet"
      },
      "extent": {
        "metaparameter": "n_hcspeciation"
      },
      "metadata": {
        "tags": [
          "chain"
        ],
        "note": "HCSpeciation, the national table: 2,562 rows. The NMHC-to-NMOG and NMHC-to-VOC factors, keyed the same way but by the SPECIES' pollutant-process. Its `oxySpeciation` column is zero in every row.",
        "esio_format": "parquet"
      }
    },
    "db_atbaseemissions": {
      "kind": "static",
      "source": {
        "url_template": "./movesdb/ATBaseEmissions.parquet"
      },
      "extent": {
        "metaparameter": "n_atbaseemissions"
      },
      "metadata": {
        "tags": [
          "chain"
        ],
        "note": "ATBaseEmissions, the national table: 120 rows, one per (air-toxic pollutant-process, month group). It is not a ratio and not an emission rate: it is the base fuel's toxic emission in grams per mile, and it reaches an answer only as a QUOTIENT -- the toxic's base emission over VOC's, each scaled by its own complex-model ratio. That is `FuelEffectsGenerator.doAirToxicsCalculations`, and it is how `ATRatio` gets its model years at or below 2000.",
        "esio_format": "parquet"
      }
    },
    "db_atrationongas": {
      "kind": "static",
      "source": {
        "url_template": "./movesdb/ATRatioNonGas.parquet"
      },
      "extent": {
        "metaparameter": "n_atrationongas"
      },
      "metadata": {
        "tags": [
          "chain"
        ],
        "note": "ATRatioNonGas, the national table: 21,206 rows. The toxic-over-VOC ratio for every fuel that is not gasoline, keyed by (pollutant-process, source type, fuel SUBTYPE, model-year group) -- a packed `19502000` pair this document decodes arithmetically, with no `pollutantprocessmappedmodelyear` lookup behind it. `ATRatio` and this table are appended and not chosen between: a cohort covered by both contributes both.",
        "esio_format": "parquet"
      }
    },
    "db_sourceusetypephysics": {
      "kind": "static",
      "source": {
        "url_template": "./movesdb/sourceUseTypePhysics.parquet"
      },
      "extent": {
        "metaparameter": "n_sourceusetypephysics"
      },
      "metadata": {
        "tags": [
          "drive-cycle"
        ],
        "note": "sourceUseTypePhysics, the national table: 178 rows against the 1 the execution-database copy held. What the run selects from it is in the joins.",
        "esio_format": "parquet"
      }
    },
    "db_sulfatefractions": {
      "kind": "static",
      "source": {
        "url_template": "./movesdb/SulfateFractions.parquet"
      },
      "extent": {
        "metaparameter": "n_sulfatefractions"
      },
      "metadata": {
        "tags": [
          "chain"
        ],
        "note": "SulfateFractions, the national table: 157 rows. `SulfatePMCalculator`'s split of NonECPM into sulfate, water and a residue, keyed by (process, fuel type, source type, model-year range) and adjusted by the fuel's sulfur level. It has no electricity row, and that absence is what drops electricity's EC and NonECPM from the output.",
        "esio_format": "parquet"
      }
    },
    "db_pmspeciation": {
      "kind": "static",
      "source": {
        "url_template": "./movesdb/PMSpeciation.parquet"
      },
      "extent": {
        "metaparameter": "n_pmspeciation"
      },
      "metadata": {
        "tags": [
          "chain"
        ],
        "note": "PMSpeciation, the national table: 4,606 rows. The fraction of `SulfatePMCalculator`'s residue (pollutant 120) that is each output species; this chain reads organic carbon's.",
        "esio_format": "parquet"
      }
    }
  },
  "metaparameters": {
    "n_outputRate": {
      "type": "integer",
      "default": 375,
      "description": "How many (pollutant-process, cohort) PAIRS reach MOVESOutput, summed over the run's emitted blocks. Declared here as well as in the model it mounts for the reason the numbers around it are (docs/esm-conventions.md §49.1): this is the relay that lets a per-fixture document set it. It replaces `n_outputCohort` and `n_outputPolProcess`, which between them could describe only a rectangle. 375 is `process-tirewear`'s, three blocks of 125; a run with one emitted block of 125 needs 125, `expand-fueltype-diesel` 248, `expand-sourcetype` 430 and `expand-criteria` 372. `rateSurvivorCount` recomputes it, so it is a CHECKED declaration."
    },
    "n_sourceBin": {
      "type": "integer",
      "default": 1,
      "description": "How many source bins the widest cohort of the run holds. Declared here as well as in the model it mounts for the reason the two numbers above it are (docs/esm-conventions.md §49.1): this is the relay that lets a per-fixture document set it. 1 is right for a run whose cohorts are single-binned -- a passenger car's are, and so the bin relation is that run's cohort relation row for row -- and a run that selects a light commercial truck needs 2, a refuse truck 8. `run_sourceBinsDropped` recomputes whether the value is enough, so it is a CHECKED declaration."
    },
    "n_physicsRow": {
      "type": "integer",
      "default": 1,
      "description": "How many rows of `sourceusetypephysics` the run's source types select between them -- the width of the drive-cycle axis. Declared here as well as in the model it mounts for the reason the three numbers above it are (docs/esm-conventions.md §49.1): this is the relay that lets a per-fixture document set it. The vehicle a drive cycle is computed for is keyed by (sourceTypeID, regClassID, model-year range), so 1 is right for a motorcycle or a passenger car, a light commercial truck alone needs 3, source types 21 and 32 together 4, and the five of `expand-sourcetype` 40. `run_physicsRowsSelected` recomputes it and `run_physicsRowsDropped` says whether it is enough, so it is a CHECKED declaration."
    }
  },
  "models": {
    "Onroad": {
      "ref": "./onroad/model.esm",
      "bindings": {
        "n_outputRate": "n_outputRate",
        "n_sourceBin": "n_sourceBin",
        "n_physicsRow": "n_physicsRow"
      }
    }
  }
}
